Third-party material
--------------------

Runtime dependencies (installed separately, not bundled)
  docextract-core (Apache License, Version 2.0) -- the shared hashing and strict JSON codec
  this package's records are encoded through.

Optional dependencies (installed separately, not bundled)
  word-extract (Apache License, Version 2.0) -- the `emailextract[word]` extra; DOCX routing.
  form-extract (Apache License, Version 2.0) -- the `emailextract[form]` extra; PDF/XLSX routing.
  olefile (BSD 3-Clause), https://github.com/decalage2/olefile -- the future .msg reader
  (Phase 1b). Not a dependency of this release; no GPL dependency is allowed anywhere in
  this repository, including optional extras and development dependencies.

Development dependencies (installed separately, not bundled)
  pytest (MIT)

The test fixtures under fixtures/ are synthetic and contain no real customer, third-party or
employer data. Real email never enters the repository: fixtures/real/ is git-ignored, probes
print structure only, and no real message content is ever written to a test, a log or a commit.
